(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "2608290938")
  (:adr/title "kotoba.cloud security-first copy and localized public routes")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-29")
  (:adr/supersedes "2608281921-copy-and-localization-only")
  (:adr/body "## Context\n\nADR-2608281921 established kotoba.cloud as the identity and deploy-control entrance while keeping Kotobase storage, Murakumo compute, and Itonami agent work as separate authorities. Its first public headline, 「ことばから、実行へ。」, did not express the current kotoba-lang.org thesis: AI agents may write freely, while Kotoba makes authority and effects part of the admitted computation.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe public thesis is 「AIは自由に書く。Kotobaは境界を引く。」 / “AI writes freely. Kotoba draws the boundary.” The next sentence narrows the Cloud role: language admission checks types, effects, capabilities, resources, and target support; Kotoba Cloud carries that boundary into Passkey identity and service discovery without replacing the compiler, verifier, provider, host enforcement, key custody, or OS isolation.\n\nJapanese remains canonical at /; English is canonical at /en/. Both routes are rendered from one pure CLJC structural view and locale catalogs with the same key contract. Pages publish canonical, hreflang=ja, hreflang=en, and hreflang=x-default links, use locale-specific Passkey return URLs, and ship finite localized 404 documents. Additional languages extend the locale registry; they do not fork structure, authority boundaries, evidence status, or negative claims.\n\nThe previous ADR remains authoritative for domain roles, Passkey RP separation, discovery fail-closed behavior, host-only cookies, and hostedApply: false.\n\n## Consequences\n\nThe language and Cloud sites tell one security-first story while keeping their responsibilities distinct. Translation parity becomes testable. A localized page may not strengthen an evidence claim or imply that discovery is delegation, that AI-written code is trusted, or that all related services form one trust domain.")))
